A||||22||maryjane||Life's most embarrassing moments||||5||
Z||000000||maryjane||11-03-2001||03:26 PM||||Let's see who can best poke fun at themselve's. Anone with the courage to start it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||11-03-2001||03:40 PM||||Hmm.... where to start?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Worst one was on the road to BC, and we stopped at a campground/picnic/beach area.<BR>Went for a swim... swam out to a diving dock. Brother and cousin were messin' around. got in the skermish... somehow, un-beknowest to me, my drawstring snapped when I hip-tossed my brother off the ledge. He cam up sputtering, vowing revenge, so I did a perfect jackknife dive into the water... Needless to say, only my shorts surfaced immediately  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>The water was murkey, so I wasn't that concerned. unfortunately, my brother is a much faster swimmer than I am, so after busting a gut for a couple of moments, he dived in and grabbed the shorts... I wasn't amused. Even worse when he started swiming ashore. D-OH! He ran up the beach, and hung my  swimsuit from a branch on a tree. Beach wasn't busy, but it was populated. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Face flaming, but head held high, I walked leisurely up the beach, grabbed my trunks and walked back into the water, where I promptly dressed. Then I ran after my brother and gave him the charlie-horse of his life  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-03-2001||03:56 PM||||Not too embarrassing..but AWKWARD!<P>I met this chick one night at the clubs, she gave me her number, she remembered *my* name, but for the life of me, I couldnt remember her name..I thought her name would come to me, but  it didnt!!  <P>my roommate at the time knew I didnt know her name, so he was having a great laugh at this, whenever she called and he answered, he would'nt ask "whos calling?"  I kept begging him to ask who is calling, but he wouldnt... <P>She was superhot ,a nurse and loved my fiero, so I didnt want to ruin it.. ON our forth date, we ran into some of my friends...  Ever try to introduce a woman to your friends and you cant remember her name?? NOT FUN  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Our relationship sorta fizzled after that night  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||hugh||11-03-2001||03:59 PM||||I do truck refrigeration as well as commercial.We had a utility truck set up to use as a platform when working on trailers and I needed something from my truck,I  couldn't find it.I stood there and looked around till I realized that I was standing on it.DUH!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||11-03-2001||04:10 PM||||Since I started this, I feel obligated to submit. Went to a New Year's Eve party a few years ago, got WAY too drunk. Jane drove us home, about 3am, but I wouldn't get out of the Cherokee. I kept telling her tto leave me there. About daylight, I managed to crawl to the sidewalk, but that was it. Daylight came, the neighbors all came out to see, cars stopping on the side of the road, just to see Don passed out. That was bad enough, then a few weeks later, my brother calls and tells me he enjoyed the pictures Jane sent.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/passedout_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroKyle||11-03-2001||04:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Since I started this, I feel obligated to submit. Went to a New Year's Eve party a few years ago, got WAY too drunk. Jane drove us home, about 3am, but I wouldn't get out of the Cherokee. I kept telling her tto leave me there. About daylight, I managed to crawl to the sidewalk, but that was it. Daylight came, the neighbors all came out to see, cars stopping on the side of the road, just to see Don passed out. That was bad enough, then a few weeks later, my brother calls and tells me he enjoyed the pictures Jane sent.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/passedout.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Holy **** , I can't top that one. Thats too fricken funny. I was just gonna go with the one time I got pulled over by a cop in my underwear in the Fiero for speeding 42 in a 25. Luckily I didn't get a ticket, I was wearing a shirt though. Had to drop my sister off at a park to go meet her boyfriend.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||11-03-2001||04:22 PM||||ROFL<BR>AAAAAAHAHAHAHAHAAAAAAAAAHAHAHAA<P>Hey Don! Your jacket looks a little stained  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||JSocha||11-03-2001||06:50 PM||||Happened back in 86 in Grand Forks while attending UND (18 and dumb).<P>Went over to some girlfriends place at the girls dorm with a case of Bud.  There were a couple of basers there that they had invited that they had met another night at a party.  We were drinking in their room and one of the girls I went over to see asked me if I wanted to dance.<P>As we were dancing in her room, the basers were over by my beer.<P>Well, started drinking some more of the beer I had brought and every time I would be dancing, the basers were over by my beer.  At that time, I could drink a case by myself no problem.  But shortly after we had several dances, it became the last thing I remember.<P>Next morning, I woke up in a jail cell feeling like somebody was sitting on top of me as I could hardly move.  Blanket wrapped around me.  I open the blanket---no clothes underneath.  Absolutely stark naked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Then I find out that the cops had found me on Washington Avenue (busiest street in Grand Froks for teens and others to cruse), stuffed in an overturned garbage can right in front of McDonalds, butt naked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>I called my so called girl friends at their dorm to have them bring me back my clothes and they were laughing the whole time I called and asking me what I was talking about and why I had left.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Then I called my suite mate at the dorm, explained the situation, where I was and how to get into my room to get me some clothes and that I needed a ride as well.  He came down to the station, I got dressed and he laughed at me all the way back to our dorm.  Next day, clothes were in a bag down at Wilkerson waiting for me to pick them up.<P>Never talked to the girls thereafter, was out the rest of my beer and my suite mates and room mate got a huge laugh at it as well and would tell me to watch out for garbage cans around McDonalds every time I would head out to a party.<P>Cops had a good laugh as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||maryjane||11-03-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>ROFL<BR>AAAAAAHAHAHAHAHAAAAAAAAAHAHAHAA<P>Hey Don! Your jacket looks a little stained   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, it was. Missed New Years Day altogether, spent all of it in the bathroom, callin Rolf on that big white phone. She said she considered turning the water hose on me, but it was froze solid; I was too. Haven't touched tequila since and not much of anything else. Not real proud of this, but it happened, Jane shows it to everyone that comes around, so doesn't matter if I post it here I guess. Glad she was there to drive me home.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mach10||11-03-2001||08:46 PM||||it's all good... In return, i'll tell you my most <I>awkward</I> drinking experiences:<P>When i've had "enough" I tend to blackout and go horizontal. <BR>First time this happened I was on a flight of stairs. Came to, and was yelling loudly "Why the **** am I onnnn the floorr? Whyzz my arm hurt so much? Wha? fell downdstairz? hol'**** !"<BR>Second one of note was at a cabin party. I was 9/10s of a way through a case, sitting around the fire, drying slowly from the first round of hazing. Had a McDonalds juice cooler of water dumped on me. I blacked out. when I came to, i was in a ring of people in the middle of a fight with a MUCH larger opponent. AND I was winning... Then I stopped, and asked what the hell I was doing, and why did I have blood on my face and hands. I blacked out as I saw the guy coming back at me, and my friends jumping on the both of us.<BR>Turns out they wanted to tie me to a tree and dump the jug on my again. I had decided that I didn't want this, so i would up and cold-cocked the first one to get near me. knocked him flat. Then he got up and the fight started... Came to after the fact complaining about sore ribs and a fat lip... me and the dude were on great terms afterwards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Nothing like a friendly fist-fight to ease relations, huh?<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000010||onfire||11-04-2001||03:19 PM||||I was at a Christmas party a few years ago. It was me and about 5 other people standing in a circle. I had a beer in one of those red party cups. It slipped out of my hands, did acomplete 360. Landed right side up and splashed everyone. I wasn't that drunk. Really.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000011||Spektrum-87GT||11-04-2001||04:44 PM||||well, this was both embarrasing and downright mean, i got a taste of how mean the world can be right when i turned 15.<P>i had(and still have the occasional flare up) of dandruff... which has been a complete pain as far as i can remember, i have the type that there is no shampoo for... so i have to live with it. so here's my story about ONE incident. i'm not racist, but will be quoting some things that were said.<P>i was at the dmv standing in line getting ready to take my permit test. and this hood rat chick was standing behind me talking with her boyfriend. i was minding my own buisness, and i hear 'oh my god, look at this white boys hair', then i figure oh great, here we go again, and then she starts saying it louder and louder, things like 'i've never seen it so bad' 'look, its snowing' 'get some head and shoulders'. the whole place was looking at me, some were laughing, some people were looking at the girl like she was stupid, which she was. i didnt say anything, i figured she was trying to get a rise out of me, but she didnt get it, i just ignored her. i guess dandruff can be a good thing, i've grown thick skin and can brush off(hehe) pretty much anything someone says to me.<P>not funny, but its embarrasing||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||11-04-2001||05:08 PM||||I know it, I have the same thing. I find that using a stiff wire bristle-brush on a die-grinder will take car of it nicely...<P>Best cure is daily showering with regular shampoos. Anti-dandruffs are anti-fungal shampoos, and tend to dry the scalp out, which is what is happening. I get it in fall, and for most of the winter. I hate it when it itches when I work up a sweat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Maybe I *should* go skin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000013||Brian87egotrip||11-04-2001||08:15 PM||||Back in January My wife and I bought a new suv. I went on my luch hour to go get it from the dealer. When I came back I was rewally happy about it. I walkedmin the office with a huge grin on my face. I saw my supervisor in my branch managers office so I walked in and dangled my new keys on her nose. Her back was to me and I was standing behind her. My manager gives me this WTF are you doing look. So I look at my supervisor who has now turned and looked at me. Well it wasn't her it was a customer. I turned beat red started to stutter. My manager was dying laughing at me.  I was so embarrassed. Whole office luaghed at me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||yo_sweets_babe||11-05-2001||04:49 PM||||hmmmm....i've got tons of embarassing stories, embarassing myself must be my biggest goal in life or something...<BR>anywayz, the MOST happened a couple years ago....<P>I DROVE my dad's 91 dodge dakota pickup THROUGH the garage (door and everything) and i rammed everything straight out the back wall...the truck couldn't even be moved out or else thousands and thousands of $$$ worth of fluorescent lightbulbs would come crashing down on everything... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>and the worst part of it all was, 5 minutes later, ALL of my relatives pulled up for our easter party  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>i'm NEVER gonna live it down either <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000015||yo_sweets_babe||11-05-2001||04:51 PM||||forgot to add something - the grand total of the damage was $20,000||||reg||11
Z||000016||artherd||11-06-2001||03:34 AM||||The time my buddies and myself all did a striptease for a girlfriend of ours, and they all told me they'd wear speedos too...  only they didn't... so I was the only one.<P>The worst part is, someone caught it on film... &lt;gulp!&gt;<P>They got a laugh out of it, and I did too.  Then I filled their salt shakers with pepper, and vicea-versa.<BR>SO WHO'S LAUGHING NOW?!?!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000017||artherd||11-06-2001||03:34 AM||||The time my buddies and myself all did a striptease for a girlfriend of ours, and they all told me they'd wear speedos too...  only they didn't... so I was the only one.<P>The worst part is, someone caught it on film... &lt;gulp!&gt;<P>They got a laugh out of it, and I did too.  Then I filled their salt shakers with pepper, and vicea-versa.<BR>SO WHO'S LAUGHING NOW?!?!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
